meta {
  name: Kashier webhook (SUCCESS)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{orderBase}}/payments/webhook/kashier?region=eg
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-kashier-signature: PASTE_HEX_HMAC_HERE
}

body:json {
  {
    "event": "pay",
    "data": {
      "amount": "185.00",
      "currency": "EGP",
      "merchantOrderId": "{{onlineOrderId}}",
      "kashierOrderId": "KO-12",
      "method": "card",
      "orderReference": "LOCAL-12",
      "status": "SUCCESS",
      "transactionId": "demo-tx-1",
      "transactionResponseCode": "00",
      "signatureKeys": ["amount", "currency", "merchantOrderId", "kashierOrderId", "method", "orderReference", "status", "transactionId", "transactionResponseCode"]
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  if (!body || body.success !== true) console.log("unexpected webhook response", body);
}

docs {
  # Kashier webhook (already automated — usually don't need to send this by hand)

  This endpoint is what Kashier's servers call after a checkout completes.
  Locally, Kashier can NOT reach localhost:4000 (KASHIER_WEBHOOK_URL is not
  publicly reachable), so the order stays `pending_payment` after paying.

  Easiest flow locally (does all of this automatically):
    npx tsx play/pay-webhook.ts <orderPublicId>
  That reads the order from the DB, signs the payload with the real HMAC
  algorithm and POSTs it here. Status goes pending_payment -> placed and a
  transaction row is created.

  If you really want to send this request by hand:
  - merchantOrderId = the ORDER's publicId returned by POST /orders
    (the "02 - Create order (Kashier online)" request already saves it into
    {{onlineOrderId}}).
  - Replace transactionId with something unique per payment — retries with the
    SAME transactionId are de-duped as already-processed.
  - Fill `x-kashier-signature` with HMAC-SHA256(key = KASHIER_API_KEY from
    backend/.env) over the signatureKeys fields, sorted alphabetically,
    concatenated as `key=encodeURIComponent(value)&...`
    (copy the signing snippet from backend/play/pay-webhook.ts).
}
